ement HumanSize -- convert int64 bytes to human-readable string with K/M/G/T suffixes; when HumanSizeOpts.Binary is true use 1024-based units (Ki/Mi/Gi), otherwise use 1000-based (K/M/G)\n      - id: R2\n        text: Implement color functions -- FileTypeColor returns ANSI escape for file mode (directory, symlink, executable, etc.); Reset returns reset escape; ColorEnabled checks IsTerminal on writer; SetColorEnabled/ResetColorEnabled override auto-detection\n      - id: R3\n        text: Implement alignment functions -- PadRight pads string with trailing spaces to width; PadLeft pads with leading spaces; Columns arranges entries into rows filling terminal width\n      - id: R4\n        text: Columns must calculate column widths from the longest entry in each column and distribute entries top-to-bottom then left-to-right (matching GNU ls -C behavior)\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"ColorEnabled uses pkg/sys.IsTerminal to detect whether the writer is a terminal\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"SetColorEnabled stores override in a package-level variable; ResetColorEnabled clears it back to auto-detect\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"HumanSize rounds to one decimal place and omits the decimal for whole numbers\"\n      - id: D4\n        text: \"Import constraints: may import pkg/sys. Must not import any cmd/ package.\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: go build ./pkg/format/... succeeds with no errors\n      - id: AC2\n        text: go vet ./pkg/format/... reports no issues\n      - id: AC3\n        text: HumanSize(1024, HumanSizeOpts{Binary:true}) returns \"1.0Ki\" or equivalent per SRD\n      - id: AC4\n        text: FileTypeColor returns distinct ANSI codes for directories, symlinks, and executables\n      - id: AC5\n        text: Columns distributes entries into balanced columns that fit within the given terminal width\n```\n\n4 tasks proposed for release 00.0 (foundational infrastructure). Once these complet